# Stay inside the design system

Every UI change reuses what already exists. Do not invent parallel styling.

## Tokens only

Colors, type and spacing come from `src/styles/globals.css` (`@theme`) and `src/tokens/`.

- Colors: `brand-black`, `brand-white`, `brand-muted`, `brand-accent-blue`, `brand-accent-yellow`, `brand-line`, `brand-link`. No new hex values.
- Type: `text-h1|h2|h3-{desktop,mobile}`, `text-text1|text2-{desktop,mobile}`, `text-breadcrumbs`. No arbitrary `text-[20px]`.
- Fonts: `font-serif` headings, `font-mono` labels/meta/UI, `font-ukraine` body copy.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — off-system color and size
<h2 className="text-[28px] text-[#333]">Title</h2>

// ✅ GOOD
<h2 className="font-serif text-h2-mobile md:text-h2-desktop text-brand-black">Title</h2>
```

## Components before markup

Reuse `Button`, `Tag`, `Link`, `TextField`, `Select`, `Pagination`, `Breadcrumbs`, card
components, `SiteHeader`, `Footer`. Shared behaviours live in `.satr-*` classes
(`satr-squircle`, `satr-tag`, `satr-link`, `satr-hover-underline`) — use them, don't reimplement.

Need something new? First extend an existing component with an optional prop that keeps the
current default appearance. Only add a component when no existing one fits, and give it
`index.ts` plus `*.stories.tsx` like its neighbours.

## Non-negotiables

- No new runtime dependencies or CSS frameworks.
- WCAG 2.2 AA holds: contrast, visible focus, ≥44×44 targets, correct heading order,
  links vs buttons, keyboard support.
- Every component change is verifiable in Storybook (`npm run storybook`).
